 "text": "..title\nA resolution authorizing the employment of Thomas H. Lee as Special Counsel and Legislative Services Division Director for the Metropolitan County Council.\n..body\nWHEREAS, Section 8.607 of the Charter of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County provides that when the interests of the Metropolitan County Council (\"Council\") require legal counsel, the Council may, by resolution, authorize the Vice Mayor to employ such legal counsel under such terms and conditions as the Council may approve by resolution; and\nWHEREAS, it is in the best interest of the Council to employ Thomas H. Lee as a full time Special Counsel and Legislative Services Division Director (“Special Counsel”) of the Metropolitan Council Office.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1. That the interests of the Council require legal counsel, and the Vice Mayor is hereby authorized to employ Thomas H. Lee as Special Counsel.\nSection 2. That Thomas H. Lee shall, in addition to providing services as Special Counsel, serve as Legislative Services Division Director.\nSection 3. That the Employment Contract, attached hereto and incorporated herein by reference, by and between the Metropolitan County Council, Angie E. Henderson, Vice Mayor, and Thomas H. Lee, is hereby approved.\nSection 4. That this Resolution shall take effect from and after its adoption, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis resolution would authorize the employment of Thomas H. Lee as Special Counsel and Legislative Services Division Director of the Metropolitan Council Office. \n\nAccording to Metro Charter section 8.607, the Metropolitan Council (“the Council”) may authorize the Vice Mayor by resolution to employ a special counsel under such terms and conditions as the Council may approve.\n\nAn employment contract between the Vice Mayor and Mr. Lee provides that Mr. Lee would manage the Legislative Services Division of the Metropolitan Council Office, research and advise on legislative matters, draft ordinances and resolutions that comply with local, state, and federal law, attend meetings of the Council and its committees, render legal opinions, and review all contracts, leases, and documents submitted to the Council for approval.\n\nThe contract states that Mr. Lee’s term of service would begin no later than December 14, 2026. The contract would expire on December 14, 2029. The contract may be terminated by the Council through an affirmative vote of a two-thirds majority of the whole membership of the Council. Mr. Lee may also terminate this agreement upon 60 days’ written notice to the Vice Mayor.\n\n"
}
